add("Z0981","nothing","Fixing x (or s=y+z) turns the square condition on the discriminant into a conic with a rational base point, which just re-parametrises the factorisation (ay−b)(az−b)=b²; a Pell family needs a second prescribed relation (see Z0996). Derivation by hand, no CAS check.",["scripts/z52d_p2_TO4_residual.py"],"Symbolic verification by CAS not run.","Only the y=z−h slice (Z0996) produces a Pell-type equation.")
