add("Z0994","nothing","At ℓ∤4p with sorted valuations α≤β≤γ of x,y,z the minimal pairwise term xy (or the xz/yz pair) is unique unless β=γ, so v(xy+yz+zx)=α+β+γ forces either all valuations zero or a cancellation at the minimum; this gives the balanced-pattern restriction only.",[],"Full table of valuation patterns not enumerated.","Enumerate balanced patterns with ℓ=2,3 cancellation.")
add("Z0995","nothing","The Newton polytope of F=4xyz−p(xy+yz+zx) is the unimodular tetrahedron on (1,1,1),(1,1,0),(0,1,1),(1,0,1) (edge determinant ±1) with no interior lattice points; F is linear in z, so z=pxy/(4xy−p(x+y)) eliminates it directly.",[],"No CAS elimination-order timing test.","None needed.")
