add("Z1622","covered","The C-form with C and the shifted statement 'p+u has a divisor ≡−1 (mod 4u)' are the same: u=(a+1)/(4C) gives a bijection (cform_iff_shifted). The parametrisation p=4Cuv−u−v (a=4Cu−1, b=4Cv−1) is the same algebra; the Lean file proves the equivalence, not this identity.",["lean/ES/ES/Basic.lean:272 (cform_iff_shifted)","LEAN_Z1546.md §cform_iff_shifted"],"Specific p=409 table not written.","None.")
add("Z1623","covered","The C-form statement ES(p)⟸∃u with a divisor of p+u ≡−1 (mod 4u) is an exact equivalence (cform_iff_shifted: ∃C,a CForm ⟺ ∃u,f: f|n+u ∧ 4u|f+1), so ES⟸ shifted form holds with equality of certificate sets.",["lean/ES/ES/Basic.lean:272 (cform_iff_shifted)"],"Hall–Tenenbaum divisor literature not searched.","None.")
add("Z1624","interesting","Exact reparametrisation (proved, numerically confirmed 51/51 primes ≡1 mod 4 below 600): Type I with c=1 holds iff ∃k≥1 with kp+1 having a divisor f≡−p (mod 4k), via k=(f+p)/(4d), d=(f+p)/(4k). This is a dual shifted form (the roles of d and k swap; the modulus is 4k and the target is −p, not −1).",["scripts/z52d_p2_TO4_batch2.py"],"Only a reparametrisation; no new existence results; k<400 in test.","Test k-range larger for 2521 and 12289 (Type I-c=1 zeros for small d).")
add("Z1625","covered","The puzzle is the union conjecture of López (arXiv 2404.01508 Conjecture 1: Type A ∪ Type B covers every prime), checked to 104729; repo record B1_LINE.md §0 (I1) and FRONTIER.md.",["B1_LINE.md §0 (I1)","FRONTIER.md §3"],"None.","None.")
add("Z1629","nothing","For p=409 and C≤300 there are 128 C with a divisor ≡3 (mod 4) that is a QNR mod 409, but 0 with a divisor ≡−1 (mod 4C). The QNR/mod-4 constraints are satisfiable for many C, so the 409 obstruction is the modulus-4C congruence, not the Legendre symbol.",["scripts/z52d_p2_TO4_batch2.py"],"Near-miss scan with weaker congruences (mod 2C) not run.","Count divisors ≡−1 mod 2C for 409.")
add("Z1630","covered","T1 for the shifted form: no_shifted_square (m u f): ¬(f | m²+u ∧ 4u | f+1) is proved in Lean (lean/ES/ES/Basic.lean:245), so m²+u never has a divisor ≡−1 (mod 4u). Composite test: among 88 (n exceptional, n·m²) pairs with m∈{3,5,7}, only 2 are exceptional (n≡1 mod 4, n≤10⁵).",["lean/ES/ES/Basic.lean:245 (no_shifted_square)","scripts/z52d_p2_TO4_cform_all.c"],"Shifted form for composite n with u≤5000 not separately tabulated.","None.")
add("Z1631","nothing","Empirical symbol entropies over 2616 winning divisors: (a/p) and (−1/a) are zero-entropy (forced, Lean); (2/a) has 0.81 bits, but it is forced to +1 whenever C is even (a≡−1 mod 8); the other six symbols (a/3),(a/5),(a/7),(3/a),(5/a) are near-uniform (~1.5 bits). No new forced symbol among those tested.",["scripts/z52d_p2_TO4_divisors.py"],"Only ~8 symbols, not ~50; no conditional entropy given C-parity.","Compute conditional entropies given C mod 8 and p mod 840.")
